# Copy this file to `gradle.properties` and set the path to a JDK 17+ on your machine.
#
# Gradle 9.x needs JDK 17+ to run. If your default JAVA_HOME points at an older JDK
# (e.g. the legacy macOS Java 8), pin Gradle's JVM here so `./gradlew` works without
# exporting JAVA_HOME every time.
#
# Find a JDK path:
#   macOS:  /usr/libexec/java_home -V        (or a Homebrew path like /opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk)
#   Linux:  update-alternatives --list java  (strip the /bin/java suffix)
#
# Then uncomment and edit:
# org.gradle.java.home=/absolute/path/to/jdk-17-or-newer/Contents/Home
